    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1001">

                <pb facs="0761" n="645" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg645"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 703.4112/7.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the British Ambassador.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-05-09">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 9, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Ambassador</hi>: I beg to acknowledge
                    the receipt of your personal note of the 1st instant, in which, with reference
                    to your note of the 30th ultimo, you advise the Department that, on April 29
                    last, Sir Lionel Garden had turned over to the Brazilian Minister at Mexico City
                    the charge of American interests.</p>
                <p>In reply I beg to ask that you will be so good as to convey to Sir Lionel Carden
                    an expression of this Government’s thanks for his services in this matter.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State: <lb/>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
